Sharing code with umlmeta
-------------------------
umlmeta is MPL-2.0 as well, and the generators here were developed inside it before moving
out. MPL-2.0 is file-level copyleft: files may move between the two projects freely, provided
each file keeps its licence notice and any MPL-covered file that is modified stays MPL. No
permission is needed from either side, and no relicensing happens - both trees are MPL-2.0
throughout. The copy of the generators committed in umlmeta remains MPL-2.0 and carries the
same SPDX header.

Derived artifacts
-----------------
The generated ontology and shapes are derived from metamodel definitions published by the
Object Management Group (UML 2.5.1, UML Standard Profile, SysML v1, UAF, BPMN 2.0, SysML v2)
and from the OCL constraint text those specifications carry. Copyright in the specifications
remains with the OMG and the original submitters. The SysML v2 abstract syntax is derived
from the OMG SysML v2 specification (and, upstream, Eclipse SysML, EPL-2.0).

Nothing here redistributes a specification document. The artifacts state structure (classes,
properties, cardinalities) and carry constraint bodies as annotations so that a consumer can
trace each shape back to the clause it came from.
